The name 'Port Daddy' is silly enough that it deserves a splash. This adds
three editorial PNG variants (foggy/dramatic, bright daylight, cartoon)
each at 1920x1080 and 512x512, generated via Nano Banana Pro and on-brand
(cream/cobalt/sage/ebony). It also adds a TUI splash with hand-crafted
'PORT DADDY' block letters, a lighthouse silhouette, a sage-green beam,
and a 24-bit ANSI brand palette that falls back cleanly to monochrome
under NO_COLOR or non-TTY.

Wired into pd via:
  - pd --splash / pd splash  (explicit invocation)
  - pd init                  (onboarding flourish; --no-splash to suppress)

